      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nPreserve mid-conversation `system` messages in `/v1/messages` for native\nencoders (DeepSeek V4.1) instead of hoisting them into the leading system\nprompt when `--chat-template` is omitted. Fixes #60537.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `deepseek_v41` deployments without `--chat-template` no longer merge\n  inline system messages; prompt prefixes stay stable across turns.\n- Fallback preserved: renderers without native support still merge\n  (conservative default unchanged).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Issue repro on current code: `Default True` (wrong) / `Official False`;\n  the `True` comes from probing the missing CLI override instead of the\n  encoder's capabilities.\n- New tests: `test_native_encoder_without_cli_template_preserves` and\n  `test_no_marker_without_template_still_merges`.\n- Commands run:\n  - `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/entrypoints/anthropic/test_anthropic_messages_conversion.py -q` → **107 passed**\n  - `pre-commit run --files vllm/tokenizers/deepseek_v41.py vllm/entrypoints/anthropic/serving.py tests/entrypoints/anthropic/test_anthropic_messages_conversion.py` → all hooks passed (ruff, mypy, test-tethering, config-defaults).\n- Duplicate checks: no open PR references #60537; complements merged\n  #58754 (HF-renderer path) and is narrower than stalled draft #58772\n  (full preserve/fold redesign).\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: `DeepseekV4Renderer` extends `BaseRenderer`, not `HfRenderer`\n(`vllm/renderers/deepseek_v4.py:24`), so `_should_merge_inline_system`\n(`vllm/entrypoints/anthropic/serving.py:243`) probed only the CLI\n`chat_template` (`None` when unset) and `_detect_merge_inline_system(None)`\nreturned `True`. The registry maps both `deepseek_v4` and `deepseek_v41`\nto the shared renderer class, so renderer type alone cannot distinguish\nthem — the fix reads a `supports_inline_system_messages` capability flag\nfrom the tokenizer (set by the V4.1 wrapper, whose Python\n`encode_messages` renders mid-conversation systems in place per\n`deepseek_v41_encoding.py:297`). Absent flag → current behavior.\n`getattr(..., False) is True` keeps the check safe against mock\ntokenizers in existing tests.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
